  {
   "q_no": 17,
   "topic": "Chemical Kinetics",
   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "For the reaction $\\mathrm{2A + B \\rightarrow C}$ is given\n$[\\mathrm{A_0}]$ | $[\\mathrm{B_0}]$ | Rate\n0.1 | 0.1 | $6 \\times 10^{-3}$\n0.4 | 0.1 | $12 \\times 10^{-3}$\n0.4 | 0.2 | $48 \\times 10^{-3}$\nFind order reaction",
   "correct_key": null,
   "correct_value": 2.5,
   "correct_keys": null,
   "solution": "Rate $= k[A]^{x}[B]^{y}$\n$$\\frac{6 \\times 10^{-3}}{12 \\times 10^{-3}} = \\frac{[0.1]^{x}[0.1]^{y}}{[0.4]^{x}[0.1]^{y}}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{2} = \\left[\\frac{0.1}{0.4}\\right]^{x}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{2} = \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^{x}$$\n$x = \\frac{1}{2}$\n$$\\frac{12 \\times 10^{-3}}{48 \\times 10^{-3}} = \\frac{[0.4]^{x}[0.1]^{y}}{[0.4]^{x}[0.2]^{y}}$$\n$$\\frac{1}{4} = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{y}$$\n$y = 2$\nSo, order of reaction is 2.5",
   "marks_correct": 4,
   "marks_wrong": -1,
   "or_stem": null,
   "or_solution": null,
